{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Design Principles","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"why"}]},{"text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class","anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" generates that class for you (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<StructName>Observer"},{"text":") and wires up the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe"},{"text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous","anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers take ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"text":" and an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"text":". They never ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":", never "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"throw"},{"type":"text","text":", and never call I\/O directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back","anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" runs effects in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":" so they don’t block UI. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void"},{"type":"text","text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"4. Persistence is invisible","anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers mutate "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" properties; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" records every change in a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" debounces and drains those changesets through "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You never write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"type":"text","text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence","text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two structural patterns:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core middleware"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" for undo; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keypaths for persistence)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain plugins","type":"text"}]},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The decision rule: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"does this need to know your action type?","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If no, write core middleware and use "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to "},{"code":"Binding(get:set:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and write back on a button.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", those plugins are blind to it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries","text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" snapshots in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"text":", so it must run ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" drains changelogs in ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The recommended order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose","anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is built for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)"},{"text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@concurrent"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with ","type":"text"},{"code":"async\/await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not","type":"heading","anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux gives you a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppEnvironment"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A network layer (use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want)."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" and Swidux doesn’t care)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours."}]},{"anchor":"11-Service-shapes-protocol-when-others-implement-it-closures-when-we-own-it","type":"heading","text":"11. Service shapes: protocol when others implement it, closures when we own it","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux services deliberately come in two shapes, chosen by who supplies the implementation:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Protocol"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — when apps or vendor adapters implement the backend:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (RevenueCat, StoreKit, simulated), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Mixpanel, Amplitude, console), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsService"},{"text":" (any JSON host).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A protocol gives conformers a stable, documented contract.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Struct of closures"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — when the library owns the shape and apps only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"configure or mock it: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchService"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalChallengeSource"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SyncPreflightService"},{"type":"text","text":". Closures make the built-in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".live"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".mock"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factories and per-test overrides trivial without a conformance ceremony.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is a signal, not an accident: if you find yourself conforming to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"struct-of-closures service, that service was designed to be configured, not","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replaced."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Anti-patterns","anchor":"Anti-patterns"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Calling ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"text":" from inside a reducer — use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Owning the store with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@StateObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — use ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObservableObject"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Buffering form state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Registering ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" before ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" — snapshot must precede mutation.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"],["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"],"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"title":"Explanation","generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation"}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","title":"Effect","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","abstract":[{"text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SwiduxPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","title":"PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","title":"ChangeSet","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","abstract":[{"text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","title":"UndoPlugin","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","title":"Plugin Architecture","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"abstract":[{"text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"type":"topic","title":"Send","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","abstract":[{"text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"StateWriter"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that reads a property through the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"title":"binding(_:sending:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"binding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"KeyPath","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Observer","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sending","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Binding","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","title":"Build Your First Swidux App","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","abstract":[{"text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"abstract":[{"text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Security Posture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","role":"collectionGroup"}}}